    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking for some advice on pallet stacking for our new high-density racking system in the warehouse. we're dealing with some pretty heavy industrial loads and i'm worried about stability when we stack them high. specifically, what's the best way to handle the center of gravity and any interlocking patterns you'd recommend to keep things from shifting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To maintain stability in your high-density racking system, it's essential to focus on the center of gravity of each pallet and the overall distribution of weight. A general rule of thumb is to alternate in a \"face-to-face\" or \"skyline\" pattern, with the center of gravity as the reference point, to minimize interlocking and put the weight evenly across the rack. This pattern helps to reduce the likelihood of shifting and maintains the stability of the pallets.",
